      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi, I made the exact same observations trouble shooting stuttering after my recent upgrade from Nvidia 1070 FTW to AMD 9060 XT. \n\nCounter-intuitively running the game with launch option \"--disable-amd-stutter-workaround\" got rid of the stuttering in my case. The documentation (https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/launch-options) advice against using the flag, so the mentioned \"work around\" might be redundant in certain configurations?\n\nSpecs: openSUSE Tumbleweed-Slowroll, Linux 6.17.7-1-default, AMD Ryzen 5 3600X, AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT 16Gb, 32Gb DDR4, wired streaming with ALVR to Pico 4 Enterprise.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-01-06T20:37:01.371Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I think this may only affect AMD users so here is my Specs: Windows 11 Pro 23H2 22631.2861 (fresh install), AMD GPU driver 23.12.1, AMD GPU Radeon RX6800 16GB, AMD CPU Ryzen 7600X, 64GB DDR5 5200Mhz, Streaming to a Quest2\n\nWhen i open the UI (the square one attached to your hand or the big one) and move my head about i get MASSIVE stutters.\n\nI suspect it is images Of avatars or worlds (any) being displayed , because it seems to mostly happen when they are on screen, like if you open and close a ui wing containing them.\n\nI have checked steam vr's performance graph, ALVR and VD's performance graphs. and vrchat's own internal FPS counter, no stutters or frame drops from any of them.\n\nAnd if you have one of these images in view, sake your head wile in steam's overlay you can see the stutters are coming from vrchat. and so far all my other games works fine.",
